.TH ATRUN 1
.SH NAME
atrun \- execute due at jobs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B atrun
[\-s spool]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Scan a private queue, atomically claim due jobs and execute each with /bin/sh.
The default queue is /var/spool/at. Jobs run concurrently; atrun waits for its
workers and returns failure if any waited job fails. Standard input is
/dev/null. Output is saved in spool/output/job-id.
.PP
Multiple runners may safely inspect the same queue. A hard link in running
claims each pending file before its jobs entry is removed. Only the claimant
starts the job. Claimed jobs are not automatically replayed after interruption.
See at(1) for ownership, failure recovery and timestamp limits.
.SH SERVICE
cron invokes atrun once per minute, including when recurring crontab parsing
fails. It can also be invoked manually for immediate processing of due jobs.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 for successful processing or an empty queue; 1 for queue/dispatch/job failures;
2 for invalid arguments.
.SH SEE ALSO
at(1), cron(1)
